      "name": {
        "name": "WD repeat-containing DNA damage-binding protein",
        "short": "WD_repeat_DNA-damage-binding"
      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "This family of proteins includes members that are involved in DNA-binding and recognition of specific DNA modifications. They are known to bind to both single- and double-stranded DNA, with a preference for UV-damaged DNA, suggesting a role in DNA repair and maintenance. Some family members have been identified as specific readers of the modified DNA base 5-hydroxymethylcytosine (5hmC), which is important in epigenetic regulation. The presence of WD repeats indicates a potential role in protein-protein interactions, which may be crucial for their function in DNA-metabolic processes.",
